  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of an ideal monoatomic gas is compressed isothermally in a rigid vessel to double its pressure at room temperature, $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The work done on the gas will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lKQx8",
      "text": "\n$300 R \\ln 6$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "O5Qox",
      "text": "\n$300 \\mathrm{R}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nj9EU",
      "text": "\n$300 \\mathrm{R} \\ln 7$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1MMp4",
      "text": "\n$300 \\mathrm{R} \\ln 2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Work done on gas $=\\mathrm{nRT} \\ell n\\left(\\frac{p_f}{p_1}\\right)$\n$$\n=\\mathrm{R}(300) \\ell \\mathrm{n}(2)\\left(\\because \\frac{P_f}{p_i}=2 \\text { given }\\right)\n$$",
    "image": null
